# Line endings.
#
# core.autocrlf is on, so without this file Git checks shell scripts out as
# CRLF on Windows. `COPY docker-entrypoint.sh` then bakes "#!/bin/sh\r" into
# the image and the container dies at startup with the famously unhelpful
#
#     exec /usr/local/bin/docker-entrypoint.sh: no such file or directory
#
# which names the file it just failed to run. The interpreter is what is
# missing, not the script. Anything that ends up inside a Linux container, or
# that Docker parses, is pinned to LF here.

* text=auto

*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
Dockerfile.* text eol=lf
.dockerignore text eol=lf
.gitattributes text eol=lf

# Data and metrics files are read by pandas and csv on both platforms; pin
# them too so a diff never shows every row as changed.
*.csv text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
